| **FND-19** | `docs/ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA.md` & `docs/DOMAIN_COVERAGE_MATRIX.md` | Table 2 & G.3 | `k <= 67 for R=1,000` with lower bound `[33, 67]` | Theoretical Bonferroni FWER for $m=100$ is $q \approx 0.0488$. For $R=1,000$, $P(K > 67) \approx 4.34 \times 10^{-3} > 10^{-3}$, making $k \le 67$ overly restrictive. Imposing a lower bound is incorrect (a low FWER indicates superior control, not test failure). | `STAT_VALIDATION` | Recompute exact upper bound: $k \le 71$ for $R=1,000$ ($P(K \ge 72) = 8.2045 \times 10^{-4} \le 10^{-3}$); $k \le 20$ for $R=200$. Remove lower bounds across all documents. | RESOLVED IN PLACE |
| **FND-20** | Across multiple validation documents | Multiple sections | Bare "3 SE" band used throughout without stated aggregate false-failure budget. | A fixed 3 SE interval corresponds to $\alpha \approx 2.7 \times 10^{-3}$ two-sided, failing a $10^{-3}$ per-check budget. Tests lacked an aggregate suite-level false failure budget. | `STAT_VALIDATION` | Establish aggregate false-failure budget $\alpha_{\text{suite}} \le 10^{-2}$ per full SLOW run, with per-check threshold $z = \Phi^{-1}(1 - \alpha_{\text{check}}/2) \approx 3.29$ for $\alpha_{\text{check}} = 10^{-3}$. Replace bare "3 SE" with budget-derived $z$. | RESOLVED IN PLACE |
| **FND-21** | `docs/ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA.md` | Table 2 | `Log-log empirical slope in [-0.55, -0.45] with SE <= 0.05` | Internally inconsistent: if true slope is $-0.50$ and $\text{SE} = 0.05$, the interval $[-0.55, -0.45]$ equals exactly 1 SE half-width, causing a correct implementation to fail $\approx 31.7\%$ of the time. | `NUM_TOLERANCE` | Replace with: theoretical slope $-0.5$ must lie within $[\hat{\text{slope}} \pm z \times \text{SE}]$ with budget-derived $z \approx 3.29$, plus separate informativeness condition $\text{SE} \le 0.05$. | RESOLVED IN PLACE |
